# Site additions to proxy/filter — one hostname pattern per line, one reason each.
# Appended to the upstream filter at build time (proxy/Dockerfile, named context `site`).
# Each line is ^...$ built from a-z 0-9 - \. and, for a rotating label, [a-z0-9.-]+
# followed by at least two literal labels; anything else (|, (), *, a bare dot) fails
# the proxy build and scripts/doctor.sh, because one regex can allow every host
# (proxy/check-filter.sh has the grammar).
# The proxy is the agent's only path out, so this file IS the site's egress policy:
# the forge (SSH and API), the notification push host, anything else the site's
# work needs. Upstream already lists the relay, claude.ai, platform.claude.com,
# github.com, api.github.com and the registries. Examples, commented out:
#
# A self-hosted forge (site.conf FORGE_SSH_HOST / FORGE_API_BASE):
^git\.example\.internal$
#
# The notification push host (site.conf NOTIFY_URL):
#^ntfy\.example\.org$
#
# GitHub Actions RAW LOG blob storage: `GET api.github.com/.../jobs/{id}/logs` 302s to a
# rotating Azure blob account; the CONNECT host is stable, so filter here, not at L3/L4.
# Wider co-tenant surface than the registries above (shared Actions-results storage) and
# tinyproxy matches the CONNECT host, not SNI — a bounded covert-egress channel. Used by
# scripts/gh-actions-log.mjs.
#^productionresultssa[0-9]+\.blob\.core\.windows\.net$
#
# Docker Hub web/API for a read-only post-release spot-check (not an image pull path):
#^hub\.docker\.com$
